## Development Workflow (After Spec is Ready)

Once spec is approved (`/spec-review` passes):

```
1. /module-start NN-slug
   ↓ Creates feature branch + scaffolds src/ folder structure

1.5 (OPTIONAL — automated execution) /module-run NN-slug
   ↓ Invokes `module-orchestrator` agent which automatically dispatches
     supabase-engineer → logic-engineer → layout-architect → qa-validator
     for every pending AC in tasks.md, with auto-retry 1x per technical failure.
   ↓ Updates tasks.md + _progress.md + orchestration-log.md after EVERY phase
     (so interruption at any point preserves real state on disk).
   ↓ Triggers /module-test + /sec-audit at the end and stops before /module-complete.
   ↓ Use when spec/tasks/security are mature and you want to reduce manual hand-off.
   ↓ Use `--dry-run` to preview routing, `--from AC-XX` to resume after halt,
     `--no-qa` to stop before the QA gate.
   ↓ See .cursor/agents/module-orchestrator.md and .cursor/commands/module-run.md.

2. TDD Cycle (per acceptance criterion):
   a. RED: Write failing test (unit, integration, E2E)
   b. GREEN: Implement minimum code to pass
   c. REFACTOR: Clean, extract, integrate with state/components
   d. SECURITY: Run security audit; check against 15 Laws
   
   Update tasks.md checkboxes as you complete each phase
   (skip this step if you used /module-run in 1.5 — orchestrator handles it)

3. /module-test NN-slug
   ↓ Run Vitest (browser-mode) + Playwright E2E + axe accessibility
   (skip if /module-run already triggered the QA gate)

4. /sec-audit NN-slug
   ↓ Verify all 15 Laws; check RLS policies; validate Zod schemas; check logs
   ↓ Mark security.md as "Verificado"
   (skip if /module-run already triggered the QA gate)

5. /module-complete NN-slug
   ↓ Merge to main; update _progress.md to "Pronto"
   (ALWAYS human gate — never invoked by /module-run)
```

