## Spec Review Gates (`/spec-review`)

Before marking a spec "ready for implementation", verify:

- [ ] All Gherkin criteria are executable (Given/When/Then)
- [ ] Acceptance criteria count is realistic for scope (8–15 typical)
- [ ] All upstream dependencies listed are "Pronto" in _progress.md
- [ ] Security.md maps all 15 Laws; non-applicable ones have rationale
- [ ] tasks.md has one task per criterion; RED/GREEN/REFACTOR/SECURITY phases are clear
- [ ] File structure proposal is realistic (no vague "TBD")
- [ ] Success metrics are measurable (coverage %, performance targets, security scorecard)

If any gate fails, request adjustments via `/spec-draft` questions or manual edit.

---

## Constitution & Immutable Principles

This SDD process is governed by `specs/_constitution.md`, which defines:

1. SDD always comes first
2. TDD cycles strictly on real DOM (Vitest browser-mode + Playwright)
3. One module at a time (no parallel features)
4. Multi-tenancy baked in from day 1 (RLS, household_id)
5. Security is zero-trust (never assume client is safe)
6. Tests execute in real browser (no mocks of DOM)
7. Fixed module order (no skipping or reordering)
8. Specs are living documentation (update as you learn)
9. Tests are the spec's executable contract
10. Strict TypeScript (no `any`, exhaustive checks)

**Breaking SDD = breaking the entire build process.** All agents and commands enforce this strictly.

